# ── Web env docs ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vite loads .env.development for `pnpm dev`, .env.staging for
# `pnpm build:dev` (--mode staging), .env.production for `pnpm build`.
# Only VITE_* vars are exposed to the browser.
#
# Copy the per-env file you need and fill placeholders:
#   cp .env.development.example .env.development   (usually not needed — committed defaults are fine for local)
#
# Vars:
#   VITE_APP_ENV=development|staging|production  Shown as a badge in the UI.
#   VITE_API_BASE=/api  (local dev, uses Vite proxy) OR
#                 https://<your-worker-host> (Pages build, direct to Worker)
#   VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8787  (dev-server only, which Worker to proxy /api to)
#   VITE_MOCK=true|false  (true = placeholder data, no backend needed)
